 "method": "W7-STAGE2 material layering for the train-car and ground pages (facade-v3-architecture/s2c_material_layering.py style;\nlane-s2, claude-einhander).\n\n1) swatches: JuggernautXL v9 txt2img 1024 (core nodes, 32 steps, cfg 5.5, dpmpp_2m karras) -> made tileable by a\n   variance-preserving four-copy sin^2 blend (the s2c offset cross-fade left a visible seam; first swatches FAILED, see\n   FAILED_SWATCHES).  The cached Stage 1 swatches were checked first and do not fit: 'painted_steel' reads as\n   vertical wood grain and 'gunmetal' has a swirl pattern; both would read as the wrong material on flat car panels.\n2) one CLUT-free modulation layer per page (8 px/texel = the 2048 grid, float16): the swatch luminance is tiled at\n   REPEAT_PX per repeat; high-pass (luma - gaussian 24 px) normalised to ~[-1,1] and band-limited (gaussian HP_BLUR_PX,\n   motion) + low-pass mottling; factor = 1 + k_hp * 0.35 * clip(hp) + k_lp * clip(lp) (s2c formula).  Strength is 0 within\n   EDGE_TEX texels of the page's transparent texels (silhouettes stay exact) and 0 on protected painted lettering\n   (1BC35EBE marking + emblem: the bright glyph indices inside uv [64,96,128,128], dilated 1 texel, feathered).\n3) per drawn static key: RGB = frozen v2 export RGB x factor (alpha untouched, class re-validated at every native texel\n   centre on re-read); 1024 = box-down of the 2048 result (s2master.export).\nusage: python -I mat_layer.py swatches | build <run> | review <run>",
 "supersedes": "stage2-sky-ground-v2 RGB of the three 6AE78470 keys only (alpha bit-identical to v2). 65560E82-83E366BC (girder strip / sky page) stays in stage2-sky-ground-v2, not layered.",
